{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Guard</b> — Some say that שמרה is past tense like זכרה ירושלם (Psalm 137:6), [meaning] 'for my soul has guarded what is fit to guard until I become a pious one.' And Rabbi Judah ben Bilʿam said: the meaning is 'guard my soul until I am always a pious one.' But the correct interpretation: the word שמרה [governs] נפשי, like 'Guard my soul and deliver me, for I am a pious one' — and he is not a stranger, for in the psalm 'the insolent have risen against me' (Psalm 86:14), he too said 'do not give up Your pious one' (Psalm 16:10); may He requite me according to my righteousness."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 86, :notes {0 "The last phrase 'יגמלני כצדקי' is obscure; rendered hyper-literally. The implication appears to be a citation or allusion to Psalm 138:8, though the form and referent are uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:10.727626631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}